WEBVTT

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.610
It was really

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.960
just a small thing.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.300
If I just threw it away,

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.890
I wouldn't have had a problem.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:45.600
Stay still!

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.480
Nevertheless, I...

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.010
How beautiful!

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.250
It's as if a jewelry box burst open.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.210
And among its contents...

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.130
the one that shone the brightest

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.140
was a black gem.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.680
Pride, huh?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.240
This belong to you?

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.790
You protected your pride.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.050
I wanted to protect him.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.050
The jewel that's mine alone.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:15.560
A necklace heirloom of the noble family Bourban has been stolen.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.380
Despite being guarded by several hundred police,

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.120
it was stolen so easily.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:21.820
The culprit is...

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.580
...Mine Fujiko.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.070
Last month, it was a Mycenaean golden ring.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.680
She's only stealing gaudy and low-class things.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.420
Furthermore, she imitated Lupin's calling card.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.080
She doesn't know her place.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:43.590
This time it's Duchess Langley's tiara stored at the Marseine art museum.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.020
Inspector...

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.610
I've been put in charge of Fujiko.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.840
Until she's captured, I won't be allowed to pursue Lupin.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.320
I can't afford to waste time on a pawn like Fujiko.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.570
While we're tied up here, Lupin is...

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:02.610
Inspector Zenigata.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.580
I will put everything I have into apprehending Mine Fujiko.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.110
I swear this on my life.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.900
What is this mess?!

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:34.760
I tried preparing some oatmeal in tuna broth.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.560
Is it not to your liking?

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.420
What's with you?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.350
Are you trying to take care of me?

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.690
What are you after?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.200
If you want to have sex with me, don't beat around the bush!

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.280
You'll catch cold.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.490
Get out.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.390
<i>She's...</i>

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.240
<i>definitely a tramp.</i>

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.330
<i>At first,</i>

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.490
<i>I thought she was a pure woman.</i>

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.850
<i>Has my perception dulled?</i>

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.100
<i>That'd be a grievous fault for a man who follows the way of the sword.</i>

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:19.870
<i>However...</i>

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.580
<i>I can't say I was entirely wrong.</i>

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.610
<i>And now a report on the necklace that was stolen from the Bourban family.</i>

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:36.620
<i>Police received a calling card announcing intent to steal from a thief named Mine Fujiko.</i>

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:40.120
<i>This information was disclosed in a press conference at the investigation headquarters.</i>

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.020
<i>The Bourbans necklace and last month's...</i>

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:46.880
<i>A woman named Mine Fujiko.</i>

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.880
<i>At least for the sake of my swordsmanship,</i>

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.140
<i>I must find out the truth about Mine Fujiko.</i>

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.390
Our security is flawless.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.890
50 around the entrance,

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.410
30 at the back,

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:07.920
and on the nearby roads and surrounding buildings, about 300 men are stationed.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.350
Not even an ant could get in, much less a rat.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.160
Gas masks on!

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.610
Tear gas distributed through the sprinkler system.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.620
It's all going as I expected.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.580
Stay focused!

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.830
Protect the tiara!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.240
Inspector...

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.040
Did Mine Fujiko not appear?

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:42.770
This is...

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:44.910
Call the expert.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.770
Have him examine the tiara!

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.570
Oh dear.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.460
<i>A perfect crime after a calling card.</i>

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:07.710
<i>It's a bit too flashy for Mine Fujiko's style.</i>

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:14.090
<i>Unlike Lupin, who steals for the thrill of it,
Mine Fujiko actually values the item.</i>

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.090
<i>She wouldn't purposely do something dangerous.</i>

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.830
<i>There are four possible points from which she could've entered the area.</i>

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.290
<i>But there are no signs of her breaking in.</i>

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.180
<i>So basically,</i>

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:26.600
<i>that's not when the tiara was stolen.</i>

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>I can only assume she swapped the tiara with a fake beforehand.</i>

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.860
<i>However, that museum has been closed for a week since we received her calling card.</i>

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:39.790
<i>We had the tiara examined two days before the theft,</i>

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.620
<i>and it was confirmed to be authentic.</i>

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:49.500
<i>And at all sites of the stolen objects, Mine Fujiko's hair and fingerprints were found.</i>

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.130
<i>It's as if she purposely left clues.</i>

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.720
<i>What a farce.</i>

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.660
<i>This is definitely...</i>

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.340
<i>...a crime committed from within the police department.</i>

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.290
<i>In that case...</i>

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:06.300
Inspector Zenigata, we've received a new calling card from Mine Fujiko!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:13.390
This time she's stealing Marie Louise's engagement ring from the Pissaro Museum of Archaeology.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.340
Oscar.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.400
You said that you'd swear your life to capturing Mine Fujiko.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.400
Y-Yes.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.260
Then I'll leave it to you.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.260
Please wait!

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:28.400
If you don't bring Mine Fujiko's case to a close, Lupin will...

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.630
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.780
<i>Why...</i>

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.620
Why is Inspector Zenigata...

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:39.790
There she is!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:40.890
It's Mine Fujiko!

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:42.370
Don't let her get away!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.370
<i>Why isn't he trying to capture her?</i>

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.330
<i>Why...</i>

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.040
<i>isn't he trying to kill her?</i>

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:53.340
Over there!

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.790
A-Assistant Inspector Oscar?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.370
"Why," huh?

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:03.720
I get it now.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:09.110
Maybe he'll change his attitude if Mine Fujiko kills someone.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.930
What was that?

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.320
Make sure she doesn't escape!

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.380
Oscar.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.670
Do not be alarmed.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.870
We are your allies.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.170
An owl?

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.130
I've done some research on you.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:41.340
Without any living relatives, you were taken in by Zenigata,

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.930
and attained the rank of Assistant Inspector.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:48.050
Your respect and affection for Inspector Zenigata

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:50.910
eventually transformed into love and violent passion,

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.230
and now you've become a murderer.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.950
Don't mock me!

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:00.160
<i>You want him to come running after you.</i>

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.280
Stop it.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.250
<i>That being the case,</i>

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.400
<i>it would've been better to disguise yourself as Lupin.</i>

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.180
<i>Why did you disguise yourself as Mine Fujiko?</i>

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:10.620
Shut up, you blasted bird!

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:17.300
<i>You wish to receive from Zenigata what Mine Fujiko received in that interrogation room.</i>

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.450
<i>Drenched in sweet obsessions,</i>

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:22.800
<i>they feverishly engaged in </i>that<i> relentless activity—</i>

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.390
Shut the hell up!

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.600
<i>I will aid you.</i>

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.260
<i>Just as you want,</i>

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.400
<i>in the way you want it,</i>

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:36.730
<i>at the place you want to reach...</i>

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.240
<i>the Bride of Fear.</i>

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.750
On the weekend of the Revolution Festival,

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.180
Mine Fujiko's calling card came.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.290
At the center of the parade

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:11.220
is this year's "bride", representing a virgin married to the ideal of revolution.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:15.680
Mine Fujiko's target is the bride's dress.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:20.370
That dress is studded with precious gems from all around the world

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.340
that compete against each other with their brilliance.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.290
In fact, they shine so brilliantly that any bride would be overshadowed.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.890
Today, in the place of Inspector Zenigata,

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.170
I will take command!

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.650
I knew it.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.120
<i>This is a follow-up report.</i>

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:38.680
<i>Mine Fujiko is believed to be behind the incident involving Marie Louise's engagement ring,</i>

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:42.930
Men may act nice, but in the end they're all...

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:43.600
<i>Mine Fujiko is believed to be behind the incident involving Marie Louise's engagement ring,</i>

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:49.340
<i>and seems to have fled the scene after shooting a policeman to death.</i>

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:50.870
M-Me?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:55.830
<i>This crime uses a different trick than the one to steal Duchess Langley's tiara.</i>

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:56.200
Tiara...

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.350
<i>and is unusually brutal...</i>

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.830
I will crown you with a tiara.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:20.680
<i>The authorities have expressed deep concerns over Mine Fujiko's crimes</i>

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.910
<i>and assigned additional manpower to help resolve the case as soon as possible.</i>

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.720
I have to kill her.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.420
I have to kill Mine Fujiko.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.480
Count Almeida.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.740
A new page in the story of Mine Fujiko

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:41.740
is about to be written.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:44.240
I'll have one.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.420
You can't fight a war on an empty stomach.

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:53.430
Lemme get one.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.630
<i>Well now.</i>

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.010
A bomb threat?!

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:07.790
It says that a bomb is hidden somewhere in this town.

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:11.070
Don't you think she's just trying to confuse us?

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:15.400
<i>The revolutionary festival is of great meaning to the people.</i>

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:18.620
<i>We can't afford to cancel the parade.</i>

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:23.190
Mine Fujiko, what are you thinking?

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:25.530
She's not thinking anything.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.380
Inspector Zenigata?

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:31.160
Mine Fujiko isn't behind this.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:34.860
She wouldn't do this.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:35.950
What?

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.800
Her criminal history...

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.640
Going by the pattern of her activity,

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:45.300
the latest string of incidents can only be caused by someone else.

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:46.990
Inspector!

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.330
What are you saying?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.070
She left behind so much evidence—

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.480
I believe in what I can see.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.380
<i>...what I can see.</i>

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:58.370
I believe in Mine Fujiko.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.570
<i>He believes in Mine Fujiko?</i>

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.010
I see.

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:09.270
A parade, huh?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.830
That spittoon woman!

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:19.590
There are things that transpire only between men and women that you wouldn't understand.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:26.240
Something that you cannot understand about a person until you are connected with them.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.330
Quit messing with me!

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:29.750
We did not come to argue with you.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:34.230
We came to discuss the arrangements for the parade.

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:43.010
One after another...

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:46.240
How much more do I have to dance for you?

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.420
Have it your way.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.820
I'll play along.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.840
Start chirping, birds.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.770
<i>The revolutionary bride has reached Point S.</i>

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.590
<i>The parade will head down Chandelier Street</i>

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.660
<i>to the bridge that will serve as the main stage.</i>

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.170
<i>Just before it reaches the bridge,</i>

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:34.560
<i>there will be some spectacular fireworks.</i>

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:39.040
<i>Then to match those, a bomb will explode in the middle of the bridge,</i>

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.090
<i>destroying it.</i>

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:47.630
<i>When the people panic and the police force's movements are hampered,</i>

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:52.600
<i>you will run to the edge of the bridge to guard the revolutionary girl,</i>

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:55.610
<i>or rather, pretend to do so.</i>

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:57.710
<i>Then you will steal her dress.</i>

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:03.690
The parade isn't here yet?

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.330
The radio won't connect either.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.890
Why? Why is it taking so long?

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.560
Bad news! It's about the parade!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.130
We can't go any further!

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:24.570
What's that?

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.460
It's a ninja!

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:28.580
Slash! Slash! Slash!

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.840
Change the route!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.590
The parade will continue! Our pride as policemen is on the line!

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:49.230
Well, then.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.230
Found you.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:07.780
<i>More owls?</i>

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:12.530
<i>Man, the ones who did this sure are persistent.</i>

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.970
<i>I should disable the vibration-sensitive explosion device first.</i>

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:21.430
<i>I'll be a goner if this owl's claws touch the twig, huh?</i>

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.610
Why don't I start by trying to
hold the owl in place with glue?

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.940
I've got no obligation to defuse it,

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:32.450
but I don't like their way of doing things.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.030
I ask you to be calm.

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.160
Inspector Zenigata!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.300
We managed to get the parade to continue—

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.180
How many years has it been?

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:23.400
In this city, I was forced into something I detested.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.500
Getting involved in corruption.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.110
If I wanted to reach the top, I had no choice.

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.990
Or so I thought.

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:34.880
But it was right here

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:39.340
that I met a filthy brat who tried his best to protect his one fran coin.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:47.840
Inspector Zenigata...

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:52.440
That brat taught me a lesson.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:56.990
No matter how dirty your hands are, there are some things you should never let go of.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:03.480
No matter how small, the moment you let it go,

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:08.060
regardless of what else you obtain, it'll turn to desolate sand.

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:12.210
I reported my boss for it.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.640
I gave up my path to the top, but I don't regret it.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.140
I believe in those who hold on to pride.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.470
<i>Black...</i>

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:27.630
<i>...gem.</i>

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.480
I...

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:35.400
The thing I really wanted to protect...

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:37.990
Oscar!

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.020
<i>Pride means nothing.</i>

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.560
<i>No matter how filthy,</i>

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.280
<i>no matter how low I sunk,</i>

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.290
<i>there was something I wanted to obtain.</i>

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:52.750
<i>But...</i>

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:07.930
Not good.

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:09.540
This is gonna...

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:17.320
There's no time to defuse it!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:18.670
Hey, don't do that!

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:23.500
I...

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:25.990
was already holding it in my hands.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:28.980
Hey!

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:34.840
<i>If you say that you'll believe even a person like me,</i>

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:42.760
<i>then I will protect... those feelings of yours.</i>

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:06.160
<i>I obtained it.</i>

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.060
<i>The black gem...</i>

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:11.620
<i>that is mine alone.</i>
